      "a_straight_shelled_orthoconic_cephalop": "A straight-shelled (orthoconic) cephalopod. The largest reached 6-9 meters — for context, that's bigger than a great white shark. Cameroceras was the apex predator of Ordovician seas for ~40 million years.",
