      "bates_college_edmund_s_muskie_archives": "Bates College Edmund S. Muskie Archives (Lewiston) — political papers, Maine journalism history",
      "bbq_grilling": "BBQ + grilling",
      "be_careful_with_the_analogy_the_reform": "Be careful with the analogy. The Reformation was driven by genuine theological + political grievances, not just by new technology. Print accelerated trends already in motion. The same caveat applies to digital + AI: technology amplifies; it rarely creates the underlying forces. The Reformation print war is instructive about how information technology interacts with institutional change — not about whether technology by itself is the cause of change.",
