      "when_the_weld_looks_wrong_deciding_wha": "When the weld looks wrong, deciding what to do (re-weld? grind out? abort?) requires welding judgment.",
      "when_you_weld_carbon_steel_the_haz_hea": "When you weld carbon steel, the HAZ heats above 1340°F (full austenite). When you stop welding, that region cools. If it cools FAST (thin section, cold base metal, no preheat) — martensite forms in the HAZ → brittle → crack. Higher carbon content = more martensite = more crack risk. ",
      "where_each_element_is_in_weight_percen": "where each element is in weight percent",
      "whether_bidding_a_job_for_a_customer_o": "Whether bidding a job for a customer or estimating internal hours for a supervisor, welders need to translate prints into time + materials. Bad estimates = lost money OR lost bids.",
